The lofi theme's faces (~/.config/themes/lofi/). All SIL Open Font License 1.1.
Nothing here is subset or instanced: the files are exactly as upstream ships
them (sha256 below), so a later fetch can be compared byte for byte.

Nunito -- the UI face (theme.conf font=): the bar, the toolbox, the popup
    panels, the launcher, mako (Nunito SemiBold 11), Nautilus's document face.
    A well-balanced rounded sans: soft terminals, open shapes, the "round
    everything" of the theme without a display face's quirks at 13-15px.
    Kept VARIABLE (wght 200-1000): it is only the UI face, never a terminal
    face, and fontconfig exposes its named instances (Regular, SemiBold,
    Bold...) to GTK and Pango, so nothing needs a static cut. About as wide
    as IBM Plex Sans at UI sizes with slightly taller lines, so the panels
    come out within 2-3% of cyberpunk's (the measured numbers are in
    ~/.config/themes/lofi/panel.css's header).
    Files: Nunito[wght].ttf, Nunito-Italic[wght].ttf
    Source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/fonts/main/ofl/nunito/Nunito%5Bwght%5D.ttf
            https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/fonts/main/ofl/nunito/Nunito-Italic%5Bwght%5D.ttf
            (Vernon Adams, Cyreal, Jacques Le Bailly; google/fonts)
    Licence: OFL-Nunito.txt (from .../ofl/nunito/OFL.txt)

Rec Mono Casual -- the terminal face (term.font=, font_mono=): COSMIC
    Terminal, kitty, code in the LLM chat and Nautilus's monospace.
    Recursive's monospace "Casual" cut: brushy, friendly letterforms that
    match the hand-drawn lo-fi mood while staying a real code face
    (fontconfig spacing=100, mono). Upstream already ships it as STATIC
    Regular / Bold / Italic / BoldItalic, which is what COSMIC Terminal
    needs (it lists a family only with a Regular AND a Bold face).
    Files: RecMonoCasual-{Regular,Bold,Italic,BoldItalic}-1.085.ttf
    Source: https://github.com/arrowtype/recursive/releases/download/v1.085/ArrowType-Recursive-1.085.zip
            path ArrowType-Recursive-1.085/Recursive_Code/RecMonoCasual/
            (Arrow Type / Stephen Nixon). Only these four files and the
            licence were taken from the zip.
    Licence: LICENSE-Recursive.txt (the zip's ArrowType-Recursive-1.085/LICENSE.txt)

Comfortaa -- headings and little touches: the bar's clock, the cards'
    headings, the launcher's hero name, the LLM chat's titles, the mpv
    "paused · side A" card. A rounded geometric display face (Johan Aakerlund).
    NOT copied here: it is a Fedora package, aajohan-comfortaa-fonts
    (/usr/share/fonts/aajohan-comfortaa-fonts/, Light..Bold OTF). At fetch
    time: `rpm -q aajohan-comfortaa-fonts` =
        aajohan-comfortaa-fonts-3.105-0.9.20210729git2a87ac6.fc44.noarch
    If it is ever removed: `sudo dnf install aajohan-comfortaa-fonts`, or the
    upstream copy at https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/comfortaa
    (OFL). Without it the headings fall back to Nunito.

Fetched 2026-10-24. Installed with `fc-cache -f`; checked with
`fc-list : family style spacing | grep -i "rec mono"` (Rec Mono Casual,
spacing=100, Regular / Bold / Italic / Bold Italic).

